+### HH-DATA: households for everyone (2026-11-15)
+
+Plan: `docs/design/HOUSEHOLDS_PLAN.md`. Code: `core/include/doomo/household.h`, `core/src/household.c`. Tests: `core/tests/test_household.c` (50).
+
+* **The player's household (household 0)** holds up to **20 people besides the player on every platform, from the start** (`family_cap()` is 20, `FAMILY_MAX` is 20 on the GBA too, pool ids 1001..1020 everywhere). The three tiers (3, 10, 20; GBA 3, 6, 10) no longer limit it. The tier unlocks stay: their toast and the pet uplift are unchanged.
+* **Other households (1..)** hold residents only: a head and up to 20 people (the head counts), at most `HH_MAX_RECS` = 24 of them. A resident is in **one household at a time**: `household_of(id)` is 0, 1.. or -1 (alone; a lone resident costs nothing). Calls: `household_create / add / move / remove / set_head / reorder`. A head who leaves passes the head to the next member; a household left with one person is dissolved (the later numbers move up).
+* **Relations** (`HREL_*`, "a is b's ..."): spouse, partner, fiance, parent / child, step-parent / step-child, sibling, step-sibling, grandparent / grandchild, aunt-uncle / niece-nephew, cousin, roommate, pet owner / pet. One row per pair; the other side is filled in by a table (`household_rel_reverse`). Household 0 uses the old `FamilyMember.role` for the pair with the player when no row exists, so old saves and old callers keep working. Setting a relation with the player also updates the old role when one says it.
+* **The rules** (`household_rel_check`, one plain reason per refusal, `household_reason_text`): a couple (spouse, partner, fiance) and a crush need **two adults**, never kin (stated, shared parent or ancestor), the sim's romance rule both ways round, and one at a time. A parent (also step, grand, aunt-uncle) must be a grown-up and older in stage (baby < toddler < child < teen < adult < elder; the stage is all the age the game has, so an adult cannot be the parent of another adult: an elder can). No loops (nobody is their own ancestor), and a parent's parent is a grandparent, not a second parent. A minor is never a grown-up's roommate. A pet has only its owner and the owner is a person. The rulebook only reads the sim's rules, the kid-cast list and the life stages: `mature_adult_ok` and the kid-cast list are never written.
+* **New people** (`household_new_person`): the first free resident place; if the island is full, the adult with the lowest friendship level who is in no household, is no story or premade citizen, no partner and not the hero or avatar moves away ("X moved away to make room"); never a minor. If nobody qualifies: "The island is full." The new person is a fresh citizen of the stage the relation suggests, and the creator edits that place in place.
+* **Saving**: the new chunk `HOUS` (version 1, the 15th registry slot, worst case `SAVE_EXT_MAX_HOUS` = 3,584 B). Nothing is written while there are no households of two people and no relation rows (the chunk's header is skipped too: `save.c`), so an island without them saves **byte for byte as before**. An old save has no `HOUS` and loads with no households. On load every id is checked: a person who is dead, missing, in the player's household or in an earlier record is dropped; a record left with fewer than two people dissolves; rows that name dropped people, repeat a pair or break a rule (a minor spouse, a loop) are dropped. Any damaged chunk is refused whole and leaves no households (a fuzz test feeds it 4,000 damaged chunks).
+* **Memory**: GBA EWRAM +3,856 B, PS1 resident see `docs/PS1.md` "HH-DATA", Dreamcast and native: plain `.bss` (24 records x 140 B + 192 B).
+* **Not built here** (the next packages): the creator pages (HH-CREATOR, HH-REL), the sim, Talk, houses and news (HH-USE).
